+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema for its input, and that schema is handed verbatim to the providers, but until now nothing checked what the model actually sent: `ToolRegistry.execute` looked the tool up and handed the model's input straight to the executor, leaving every consumer to validate differently, or not at all. The registry now owns the check. Input is validated against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs, and a call the schema rejects fails in one predictable way: a returned `ToolResponse` the model can read and correct within the tool-round budget, never a thrown error that ends the conversation.
+
+## Statements
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema`
+  before the executor runs, and a call the schema rejects returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result`
+  describes the failure while the executor is never invoked
+  ([validated by: rejects a call missing a required property before the executor runs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L18)).
+- Input the schema accepts reaches the executor exactly as the model sent it, unknown properties
+  and all, with nothing injected, coerced or defaulted, and the executor is called exactly once
+  ([validated by: passes a valid input with an unlisted property through to the executor unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- A rejected call names the failing property path and the constraint that failed
+  ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the path and the expected type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L47)).
+- Neither the rejection text returned to the model nor any log line carries a property value from
+  the rejected payload
+  ([validated by: surfaces no property value from a rejected payload in the result or the logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L56)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at `register` time, so an uncompilable schema throws
+  from `register` with a message naming the tool
+  ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L73)).
+- A static tool's compiled schema is reused across `execute` calls rather than rebuilt per call
+  ([validated by: compiles a static schema once at register time and reuses it across execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L87)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is resolved per call and validated against the schema
+  current at that call, not a stale cached one
+  ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L121)).
+- An unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` rather than returning a rejection
+  ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L151)).
+- Inside the orchestrator's tool loop a schema rejection is fed back to the provider as a tool
+  result, so the model can correct the call on the next round and `processMessage` resolves
+  instead of throwing
+  ([validated by: feeds a rejected tool call back to the provider and completes on the corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` constraints only.
+- Validation applies to every registered tool; there is no opt-out.
